# The reason for each way a step function can return false. TotK 1.2.1.
#
# tools/ghidra/ExportReturnSites.py (in purah-protocol) numbers every exit of each step function in address order and writes return_sites.tsv,
# and the address of each exit. This file says what each exit MEANS. One line per exit:
#
#   function|ordinal|reason
#
#   function  the function's offset in the book, in hex (the first column of return_sites.tsv)
#   ordinal   the exit's number in that function (the third column; the debugger shows it as "failure mode ordinal/count")
#   reason    plain words: what was wrong. Separate several reasons with a semicolon: "the list is empty; the first name is blank".
#
# An exit with no line here is shown as "Unknown reason (failure mode 3/17)"; one with a line is shown as "Failure mode (3/17), <reason>".
# The exit's address (the "exit" column of return_sites.tsv, an offset from the image base) is always shown under it, so a new exit can be looked up.
# Editing this file does not need the module rebuilt: Prism reads it.
#
# Example (not a real exit):
# 70852c|3|AliasEntityList has more entries than the controller set has controller entities

# ---- worksheet: one line per exit. Fill in the reason after the second |. A line with no reason is shown as an unknown reason. ----


